# rhcs_cluster_rosa_hcp (Resource)

OpenShift managed cluster using ROSA HCP.

## Example Usage

{{tffile "examples/resources/cluster_rosa_hcp/example_1.tf"}}

## FIPS usage and lifecycle

Set `fips = true` during cluster creation to request FIPS-enabled cryptographic modules for the cluster.

Lifecycle caveats:
- `fips` is immutable in this resource. Changing it after creation is rejected and requires creating a new cluster.
- Red Hat documents that FIPS must be enabled before first boot and cannot be enabled on an existing deployment. See [Support for FIPS cryptography](https://docs.redhat.com/en/documentation/openshift_container_platform/4.10/html/installing/installing-fips).

## Proxy and `no_proxy` behavior

When a proxy is configured on a zero-egress cluster, the OCM API appends platform-managed AWS endpoints (S3, STS, and ECR) to `no_proxy`. The provider filters these platform-injected entries from the Terraform state so that it stays in sync with your declared configuration.

## Managing AWS tags after creation

On clusters whose control plane is on OpenShift 4.20 or later, `tags` can be updated in place.

- **Set `tags` to have Terraform manage them.** The configured map, including an empty map (`tags = {}`), is the complete set of customer tags. Tags added outside Terraform, for example with `rosa edit cluster --tags`, appear as drift and are removed on the next apply.
- **Omit `tags` to leave them unmanaged.** When the attribute is not set, Terraform does not report, change, or remove customer tags. Removing `tags` from a configuration that set it removes those tags once; afterwards they are unmanaged.
- **Before managing tags on an existing or imported cluster**, list the current customer tags and include every tag you want to keep. For example: `ocm get /api/clusters_mgmt/v1/clusters/<cluster_id> --parameter fetchUserTagsOnly=true`. Import does not copy tags into state.
- **If another system also manages the tags**, ignore them in Terraform so they are not removed:

```terraform
resource "rhcs_cluster_rosa_hcp" "cluster" {
  # ...
  lifecycle {
    ignore_changes = [tags]
  }
}
```

Machine pools inherit cluster tags unless a machine pool overrides the same key. Tag values cannot be empty, and keys that start with `api.openshift.com/` or are otherwise reserved are rejected.

